end to believe  that that's what the packers should be  doing  but the question becomes how far do you  go with that how much freedom do you  give him where is the line where you  don't want to let aaron rodgers  essentially be peyton manning where he's  running the offense on the fly based  upon whatever he happens to see or  thinks he sees so this is where the  tension is sharing now i'm a little  surprised that both leflore and rogers  are publicly talking about it i think  this is something they should keep  internal but either way we now know it's  there and it's now something that they  have to resolve at some point between  now and the start of the regular season  or during their first regular season  working together  well thank goodness they've had this  audible thing otherwise we wouldn't have  a whole lot to talk about because  this to me is the biggest story of  probably the last couple of weeks  that we're talking about and i think  everybody's talking about don't say it's  a slow time go and  okay it's not the slow time but you know  there's not many quarterbacks i would  trust to get up to line of scrimmage to  leave wide open  audible decisions  but aaron rodgers is one of them 11  years of experience a couple mvps super  bowl mvp this guy has done it and i  think he's earned that but again it's  matt leflore's team it's matt leflore's  offense how much rain is he going to  give aaron rodgers and this is yet to be  worked out between these two and they've  got to get it worked out or this thing  isn't going to work and  packers are going to be looking either  for a new head coach or moving on for  mary rogers and we certainly don't think  that's going to happen so lefleur is  going to have to make this work with  aaron rodgers to be there long term for  this team to win  and that's the awkward thing about this  shireen rogers is the one with the power  because of his contract because of the  fact that he's the most popular person  in the entire organization an  organization that doesn't have an owner  he's the owner and he's the guy who's  going to call the shots here and what's  amazing to me is  that they hired a coach knowing or at  least they should have known that he was  bringing this system to town i suspect  that during the interview  they they had some conversation about  how the offense would work mark murphy  played in the nfl hey what are we going  to do about audibles how much freedom is  aaron rodgers going to have at the line  of scrimmage to change the play well  mark i'm glad you asked that question  he's not going to have much not freedom  at all and how about we're hiring you  for the job anyway i mean this is  something that can't have caught anyone  by surprise whether it's brian gooda  koontz the gm of the team or mark murphy  the ceo who made that hire and now it's  out there it's out in the open and and  look i i know that there are some out  there who believe that i am quick to  criticize aaron rodgers and those people  may be correct but i i think that it's  fair to say  aaron rodgers taking this pub and i i  understand mike silver was there and he  talked to both guys when you read the  whole article it doesn't look as bad as  the tweet that came out last week but  still  what other quarterback would be engaged  in a public debate with his head coach  about how much freedom he has at the  line of scrimmage i can't think of  another time it's ever happened and here  it is happening in green bay with the  first new head coach that aaron rodgers  has had since he became the starter in  2008.  yeah and the question is where is this  thing headed and how's it going to work  itself out  does it work itself out in training camp  we know aaron rodgers doesn't play much  in the preseason he's going to play  probably more than he has the last  couple of preseasons but is this when  they work it out i don't know that he's  going to get enough work there i think  this is something that aaron rodgers  probably is going to work out in that  first game  when he gets up there and decides he  doesn't like either of the two plays  that were called and changes it up at  the line of scrimmage and  if it works i i think that's probably  the direction they go and if it doesn't  work matt laflore is going to say look  here's the two plays here's what we have  to do but this thing has disaster  written all over it if they can't get  together and decide what they're going  to do going into the season  and here's the other shrine the audible  thing is now a thing so we're going to  be paying attention to it the reporters  who are embedded with the packers will  be paying attention to it and if we  didn't know it was a thing maybe we  wouldn't be paying the kind of attention  we would so now here's what's going to  happen i mean and we hear all the time  coaches don't want distractions well  guess what here's a distraction from  matt lafleur in his first season as a  head coach because you're going to have  reporters looking for any evidence  talking to receivers linemen anyone to  find out whether or not aaron rodgers is  coloring outside the lines that matt  lafleur has put there for him to adhere  to and i think rogers ultimately does  win this one because what are they going  to do bench him for deshawn kaiser no  he's going to be able to do what he  wants to do but now by going public with  it it's become an issue it's been  flagged and we're all going to be paying  attention to this power play that is  going to play out one way or the other  between leflore and aaron rodgers  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

